{title: Lamp and Light}
{subtitle: Psalms 119:105}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I have not turned away from your [Eb]judgments
[Gm7]For you yourself have taught me the [Eb]way
[Bb]How sweet your promise is to my [Eb]taste
Sweeter than [Gm]honey in my [F]mouth
From your [Eb]precepts I gain under[F]standing
[Gm]I hate ev[F]ery path of false[Eb]hood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Your word is a [Bb]lamp to my [Eb]feet
A light on my [Gm7]path in the [F]night
Guiding [Eb]my steps with divine [Gm7]grace
Shining through [F]the darkness deep
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [F] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]I have sworn an oath and con[Eb]firmed it
[Gm7]To keep your righteous judgments [Eb]true
[Bb]I have been afflicted [Eb]beyond measure
LORD give [Gm7]me life according to your [F]word
Ac[Eb]cept the freewill offerings of my [F]mouth
[Gm]And teach me [F]your judgments a[Eb]gain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Your word is a [Bb]lamp to my [Eb]feet
A light on my [Gm7]path in the [F]night
Guiding [Eb]my steps with divine [Gm7]grace
Shining through the [F]darkness deep
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [F] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]Sweet honey flows into my [F]heart
[Gm7]Understanding [F]grows from your [Eb]precepts
[Cm7]Falsehood fades in the bright [F]light
Your [Gm]truth remains [F]forever [Eb]sure
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Your word is a [Bb]lamp to my [Eb]feet
A light on my [Gm7]path in the [F]night
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [F] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] | ×2
| [Eb] |
